# Every text file is LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# The golden-file tests in internal/mcp compare rendered output byte for byte.
# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF by default, which makes those
# comparisons fail on the first line for a difference nobody can see. Pinning
# eol=lf keeps the checkout identical on every platform; `text=auto` still lets
# Git detect and leave binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
